sequence":20,"significance":"major","source":null,"status":null,"text":"Assembly amendments concurred in. (Ayes 40. Noes 0. Page 5982.) Ordered to engrossing and enrolling.","time":null,"votes":[]},{"classificationRule":"ca-enrolled","code":null,"date":"2026-09-04","eventType":"enrolled","historyId":"119120624","location":"Governor","sequence":21,"significance":"major","source":null,"status":null,"text":"Enrolled and presented to the Governor at 2 p.m.","time":null,"votes":[]},{"classificationRule":"ca-approved","code":null,"date":"2026-09-14","eventType":"approved_by_governor","historyId":"119120626","location":"Governor","sequence":22,"significance":"major","source":null,"status":null,"text":"Approved by the Governor.","time":null,"votes":[]},{"classificationRule":"ca-chaptered","code":null,"date":"2026-09-14","eventType":"chaptered","historyId":"119120628","location":"Secretary of State","sequence":23,"significance":"major","source":null,"status":null,"text":"Chaptered by Secretary of State. Chapter 235, Statutes of 2026.","time":null,"votes":[]}],"affectedStatutes":[{"action":"IS_AMENDED","code":"GOV","text":"Section 83109 of the Government Code is amended to read:"},{"action":"IS_AMENDED","code":"GOV","text":"Section 85200 of the Government Code, as amended by Section 57 of Chapter 278 of the Statutes of 2025, is amended to read:"},{"action":"IS_AMENDED","code":"GOV","text":"Section 86112.3 of the Government Code is amended to read:"}],"approvedDate":"2026-09-14","chapter":{"citation":"Chapter 235, Statutes of 2026","number":"235","type":"CHP","year":"2026"},"chapteredDate":"2026-09-14","committees":[],"conditions":[],"contentHash":"16842943b0033890eb41c3b0fec2e63dd8401240d232b04a3e242ab8d7e9273b","cosponsorCount":null,"digest":"(1) The Political Reform Act of 1974 establishes the Fair Political Practices Commission and authorizes the commission to appoint officers, counsel, and employees consistent with applicable civil service laws. The act prohibits the commission from including a nonclerical position in the same civil service class as any position of any other department or agency.\n\nThis bill would instead authorize the commission to do so.\n\n(2) The act requires an individual, before becoming a candidate for a specific office, to file a statement of intention to be a candidate. The act requires an individual who intends to be a candidate for elective state office to file the statement of intention online or electronically with the Secretary of State.\n\nThis bill would expand the state offices for which a candidate must file their statement of intention online or electronically with the Secretary of State to include judicial offices.\n\n(3) Under the act, lobbyists, lobbying firms, and lobbyist employers who send any written or printed invitation to an elected state officer, candidate for elective state office, legislative official, or agency official, are required to include on the invitation or on a letter attached to the invitation a statement that “Attendance at this event by a public official will constitute acceptance of a reportable gift.” The statement must be typed, printed, or handwritten at least as large and readable as 8-point Roman boldface type, in a color or print that contrasts with the background so as to be easily legible.\n\nThis bill would increase the minimum text size of the required statement to 10-point Roman boldface type.\n\n(4) The Political Reform Act of 1974, an initiative measure, provides that the Legislature may amend the act to further the act’s purposes upon a 2/3 vote of each house of the Legislature and compliance with specified procedural requirements.\n\nThis bill would declare that it furthers the purposes of the act.","digestDate":null,"digestVersion":null,"effective":{"basis":"not_verified","date":null,"note":"No effective date is recorded in the official bill data and DemocracyHQ has not verified one. A non-urgency statute enacted in a regular session generally takes effect on January 1 after a 90-day period (Cal. Const. art. IV, § 8(c)), but a bill may state other operative dates."},"expiryClauses":[],"firstObservedAt":"2026-11-20T10:45:57Z","id":"ca-20252026-sb1432","identifier":"SB 1432","indicators":{"Appropriation":"NO","BudgetBill":"NO","Election":"NO","FiscalCommittee":"YES","ImmediateEffect":"NO","LocalProgram":"NO","TaxLevy":"NO","Urgency":"NO","UsualCurrentExpenses":"NO","VoteRequired":"TWO_THIRDS"},"introducedDate":"2026-03-05","issueTags":[{"matchCount":null,"matchedField":"official subject line","matchedText":"Political Reform Act of 1974.","ruleId":"tag-cf-1","tag":"campaign-finance"}],"judicialNote":"Legislative status does not show whether a court has blocked, narrowed or upheld any provision. Check the linked litigation, which may be incomplete.","lastActionDate":"2026-09-14","lastActionText":"Chaptered by Secretary of State. Chapter 235, Statutes of 2026.","lastCheckedAt":"2026-11-21T17:38:34Z","leadAuthors":"Introduced by Committee on Elections and Constitutional Amendments (Senators Wiener (Chair), Allen, Cervantes, Choi, and Umberg)","legislativeStatus":{"currentHouse":"Secretary of State","currentLocation":null,"currentStatus":"Chaptered","measureState":"Chaptered"},"legislativeSubjects":[],"measureType":"Senate Bill","officialUrl":"https://leginfo.legislature.ca.gov/faces/billNavClient.xhtml?bill_id=202520260SB1432","policyArea":null,"relatedMeasures":[],"selection":{"matchedField":"official subject line (latest version)","matchedText":"Political Reform Act","ruleId":"ca-select-2"},"session":"2025-2026 Regular Session","shortTitles":[],"sourceId":"ca-leginfo-bulk","sourcePublishedAt":"2026-11-16T05:26:36Z","sourceRecordUrl":null,"sponsors":[],"state":"06","stateAbbr":"CA","subject":"Political Reform Act of 1974.","title":"An act to amend Sections 83109, 85200, and 86112.3 of the Government Code, relating to the Political Reform Act of 1974.","verification":{"checkedAt":"2026-11-21T17:38:34Z","method":"automate